    "classes": "class id, '_shared' for the General page rows every class has, or '_pet' for the hunter pet's own spellbook page -> { className, spells[] }",
    "spells": "spell names only, no ranks and no tooltip text; the file answers 'does Classic Era have a spell of this name for this class?' and nothing else"
  },
  "caveats": [
    "Names only. There is no tooltip text here, so a spell whose numbers changed cannot be detected from this file: stage 11 marks a matched name 'unknown', never 'same'.",
    "Written from memory, so a missing name produces a false 'new'. Treat every 'new' as a lead, not a fact, until a sourced list replaces this file.",
    "Talent-taught abilities are deliberately absent (Aimed Shot, Mind Flay, Presence of Mind, Blessing of Kings and the rest). Stage 11 looks those up in the sourced talents.json instead and records 'a Classic Era talent of the same name exists' -- not 'now baseline', because the demo characters have points spent and may simply have talented into it.",
    "Racial abilities are absent. Stage 11 recognises them by the list row's own 'Racial' / 'Racial Passive' subtitle and by name against data/races/*.json, and points the record at data/races/<race>.json instead of diffing them here.",
    "Level is ignored. The demo characters are level 38, so their lists stop well short of these; a name here that the stream never showed is not missing data.",
    "The '_pet' bucket is the hunter pet's own spellbook page (Claw, Dive, Stay, the stances and the training passives), applied only to the hunter."
  ],
